ame></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAICHI, MASANORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORIKAWA, TATSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SOGABE, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, YOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>At least one fluoromonomer which is gaseous at ordinary temperature and pressure is stably and efficiently emulsion-polymerized in an emulsion obtained by forcibly emulsifying a water-insoluble liquid with high shearing in the presence of a small amount of an emulsifying agent. The emulsifying agent is used in such an amount that the number of particles of the water-insoluble liquid contained in the emulsion is kept substantially constant during the polymerization.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un procédé qui consiste à polymériser par émulsion, de manière efficace et stable, au moins un monomère fluoré, gazeux à température et pression ordinaire, dans une émulsion obtenue par émulsion, pratiquée énergiquement avec un cisaillement élevé, d'un liquide insoluble dans l'eau et d'une petite quantité d'un agent émulsifiant. L'agent émulsifiant est utilisé en quantité telle que le nombre de particules de liquide insoluble dans l'eau, contenues dans l'émulsion, est maintenu pratiquement constant durant la polymérisation.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not